course: dictionary
lesson: 11702
title: Attribute: a quality or a cause
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An attribute is a quality or feature that someone or something has. «Patience is a good attribute.» Patience means waiting calmly, and a person can have it as a quality. Say the noun AT-trib-yoot.
explain: Attribute is also a verb, said a-TRIB-yoot. To attribute something to a cause means to say it was caused by that. «Mia attributes her good marks to hard work.» Mia thinks hard work is the reason for her good marks.
explain: To attribute a painting, book or saying to someone means to say they made it. «This song is attributed to Sam, the music teacher.» The word to after attribute and a person's name is a clue that the sentence is about who made something.
explain: In maths and computing, an attribute is a feature you can sort by, such as colour, shape or size. If a sentence talks about sorting, check whether attribute means a feature you sort things by.
fact: An attribute (noun, said AT-trib-yoot) is a quality or feature that someone or something has.
fact: To attribute (verb, said a-TRIB-yoot) something to a cause means to say it was caused by that.
fact: «Patience» is a good attribute, which means it is a helpful quality to have.
fact: In maths, shapes can be sorted by attributes such as number of sides, colour or size.
fact: Physical attributes are features of the body, like height or eye colour.
exercise: «Kindness is a good attribute.» What is an attribute? | A loud noise | A sum of money | A type of sport | *A quality or feature that someone has
exercise: «Sam attributes his win to practice.» What does attributes mean here? | Forgets how he won | Gives his win away to a friend | *Says the win was caused by practice | Buys a new trophy
exercise: Ana sorts her socks by colour. What is colour in this sentence? | A mistake she made | *An attribute, a feature she sorts by | A kind of cloth | A size of football
test: «Tom is very patient and kind. These are his best attributes.» What are attributes in this sentence? | Places Tom likes to visit | *Qualities or features Tom has | Things Tom has lost | Pets Tom keeps at home
test: «The poem is attributed to Lily.» What does attributed mean here? | Given away to Lily | Torn up by Lily | Read aloud by Lily | *Said to be written by Lily
exam: «Rain is an attribute of the weather; we can attribute a wet day to the clouds.» Which meaning of attribute is used in the second part? | A quality or feature | A property used to sort things | To say who painted a picture | *To say something was caused by something else
